id: pm-pftgcz
title: "GH-1443: align item and history union ordering and provenance during lossless merges"
description: "Published 2026.10.10 reporter describes a lossless completed Git merge whose item/history differ in comment order and docs/tests provenance labels, causing hash drift and exact receipt refusal. Reproduce canonical equality before implementation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T18:21:52.755Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T08:22:48.169Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-12T08:22:47.133Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-12T08:22:47.133Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: Real isolated Git branches reproduce comment/test union divergence; item/history canonical order and provenance match; all values and creation/editor provenance survive; exact receipt settlement without force and byte-stable retry pass; retained reordered values are diagnosed accurately; prior abort and rebase controls remain valid
goal: project management = context management
parent: pm-gh1405
risk: high
confidence: medium
resolution: Preserve original branch event order and native collection semantics with sealed original patches; refuse scalar rebasing failures before stale positional operations can escape; accurately diagnose identified retained native context without relaxing exact receipts or command trust.
expected_result: "Every accepted union retains exact context and point-in-time attribution, while contradictory, ambiguous or non-applicable scalar projections remain unresolved for manual recovery; forced repair distinguishes retained context from genuine loss."
actual_result: "10206 tests, exact100/100/100/100 source coverage, full static quality, linked commands, Node/Bun public scalar-refusal and other SDK consumers, strict TypeScript and nine-package npx/bunx smoke pass. A behavior-only revert fails the loaded root-case assertion; restored source and prefixless/real-Git/abort/receipt controls pass. Original base and injected budgets pass."
