learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T03:25:08.923Z","harness:codex","A prior merge audit can carry index-based patches that are valid on its branch yet target unrelated entries after another union. Reconstruct branch-local collection state before projection, preserve original patches as proof, and compare final replay with the independent item driver."
  "2026-10-12T07:03:41.822Z","harness:codex","Final state equality cannot prove point-in-time history attribution. Preserve each original branch order, use clocks only between currently available events, test intermediate replays, and fail closed on contradictory or ambiguous coordinates. Diagnose identified retained native context separately from exact receipt authorization."
